# Balance summary, 2026-11-05

Tool: `node tools/bal13/summary_2026_11_02.js --road bal16-after2 --games 12 --road-games 20` (1.1.0 (2026-11-02, BAL13: with leaders)). Reference ladder: `docs/balance/ref/ref-ladder.json` (2026-11-02, 10 decks a map, rank 1 weakest .. rank 10 strongest). Road measure: `docs/balance/skirmish-pass-bal16-after2.jsonl` (the Map reference, 40 games a fight, seeds 9100 + 37g). Procedure: `docs/evaluation-protocol.md` section 4a.

**Engine:** the game as merged on this branch (includes FIX6's leaders). **Leaders:** every number here is played WITH leaders (owner 2026-11-02 21:37). The enemy decks keep their own (the game's skirmish / PRO leaders). Your seat plays the leader a player holds at the map (tools/bal13/lib_leader_2026_11_02.js leaderFor: the strongest card that may lead in the map-true pool, else the Wandering Traveller), dealt by the game's own harness since FIX6 (referenceFightSetup {leader}, dealPlayerLeader: out as soon as it can be paid); the per-map leader is in the table.

## Road totals (the Map reference, with its leader)

226 road fights: **73 in the green band** (target +/- 8), 84 within 10 points, **83 beyond 20 points**. Without a leader (the standard road measure, `skirmish-pass-bal16-after2.jsonl`): 92 green, 120 within 10, 62 beyond 20.

## Per map

(a) the ladder's mean win rate against the map's WPRO decks (its weakest decks) and its BPRO decks (its strongest), 12 games a pairing (10 decks x each WPRO / BPRO deck). (b) the weakest (rank 1) and strongest (rank 10) ladder deck against the map's road fights, 20 games a fight (the gap to the mean road target in points), beside the Map reference (40 games a fight).

Flag (owner 2026-11-02 20:19): the Map reference should win at most 15% against the map's strongest deck (BPRO-1, 40 games); "OVER" marks a map above it.

